{
  "explanation": "The source IP 203.0.113.42 conducted a systematic web reconnaissance scan, probing for common administrative interfaces like WordPress (/wp-login.php, /wp-admin/), sensitive configuration files (.env, .git/config), and debug scripts (/phpinfo.php). The HTTP status codes (404 Not Found and 403 Forbidden) indicate that while the target application is not running WordPress or exposing these specific files directly at those paths, the scanning activity confirms the attacker is actively mapping the attack surface to identify potential vulnerabilities.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Reconnaissance",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the source IP address (203.0.113.42) at the firewall or web application firewall (WAF) level.",
    "Implement rate limiting and automated IP banning for clients exhibiting aggressive scanning or enumeration behavior.",
    "Ensure sensitive files such as .env and .git directories are strictly denied access and never deployed to production environments."
  ]
}
